DTSTAMP:20260923T165336Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 9/23/2026: Reminders in Preparation for Maine
  eCourts and eFiling in Cumberland County Courts
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nReminders in Preparation for Maine eCourts and 
 eFiling in Cumberland County Courts\nDate:\n9/23/2026\nOn Monday\, Septemb
 er 28\, 2026\, the Maine Judicial Branch is expanding Maine eCourts to all
  case types in Judicial Region 2\, comprising Cumberland County Unified Cr
 iminal Docket (UCD)\, Cumberland County Superior Court\, Portland District
  Court\, and Bridgton District Court.\nAll case types -- civil\, family\, 
 juvenile and criminal cases -- will be included in the transition from pap
 er filing to electronic filing. As of Monday\, September 28\, all mandator
 y electronic filers pursuant to the\nMaine Rules of Electronic Court Syste
 ms (MRECS)\nwill be required to eFile documents in these courts. Self-repr
 esented litigants (parties who do not have attorneys) who file fewer than 
 six cases in a calendar year will not be required to eFile.\nCourt Closure
 s and Emergency Filing Procedures\nTo prepare for the implementation of Ma
 ine eCourts and eFiling on September 28\, Region 2 courts are currently op
 erating on a modified schedule and have emergency filing procedures in pla
 ce. In addition\, all Region 2 courts will be closed from 8 a.m. to noon t
 he week of September 28th. Please refer to the\nschedule of closures and e
 mergency procedures during these closings\n.\nShareFile Discontinued in Re
 gion 2 Courts\nThe ShareFile platform used in Region 2 courts will be disa
 bled for all criminal\, civil violation\, juvenile filings\, and GAL vouch
 ers\, at 2:00 p.m. on Thursday\, September 24. Starting Monday\, September
  28\, attorneys must instead use\neFileMaine\n. Please note\, attorney vou
 chers filed pursuant to the\nStanding Order regarding Payment to Court-App
 ointed Counsel\nwill continue to be accepted by ShareFile for a grace peri
 od of 60 days.\nTraining Resources\nFor attorneys and staff who are new to
 \nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13362444
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13362444
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
