BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4b4d04a1044d8e3c@role-professional-responsibility.maine-government-fee
 ds
DTSTAMP:20260909T205549Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260622
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] McCarthy v. Hernandez
DESCRIPTION:PRELIMINARY PRINT \nVolume 608 U. S. Part 2 \nPages 809–821 
 \nOFFICIAL REPORTS \nOF \nTHE SUPREME COURT \nJune 22\, 2026 \nREBECCA A. 
 WOMELDORF \nreporter of decisions \nPage Proof Pending Publication\nNOTICE
 : This preliminary print is subject to formal revision before \nthe bound 
 volume is published. Users are requested to notify the Reporter \nof Decis
 ions\, Supreme Court of the United States\, Washington\, D. C. 20543\, \np
 io@supremecourt.gov\, of any typographical or other formal errors. \nPage 
 Proof Pending Publication\nOCTOBER TERM\, 2025 809 \nSyllabus \nMcCARTHY\,
  SUPERINTENDENT\, ELMIRA \nCORRECTIONAL FACILITY v. HERNANDEZ \non petitio
 n for writ of certiorari to the united \nstates court of appeals for the s
 econd circuit \nNo. 25–748. Decided June 22\, 2026 \nIn 2017\, a New Yor
 k jury found Pedro Hernandez guilty of kidnapping \nand murdering 6-year-o
 ld Etan Patz decades earlier. At issue during \nthe trial\, on direct appe
 al\, and on habeas review were the trial court's \njury instructions conce
 rning various confessions to the crime by Her-\nnandez. When detectives fr
 st questioned Hernandez about the crime \nat the Camden County Prosecutor'
 s Offce (CCPO)\, they did so without \nfrst administering a Miranda warnin
 g\, see Miranda v. Arizona\, 384 \nU. S. 436\, and Hernandez\, a man with 
 a low IQ and a history of mental \nillness\, eventually confessed to stran
 gling Patz and dumping his body. \nThe detectives then read Hernandez his 
 Miranda rights\, and he waived \nthose rights and made a second\, videotap
 ed confession. Hernandez \nlater gave another videotaped confession to an 
 assistant district attor-\nney in New York\, and he continued to confess t
 o Patz's murder to his \nfamily\, his psychiatrist\, and others. At trial\
 , the trial court denied Her-\nnandez's motion to suppress his statements 
 to the detectives and the \nassistant district attorney. The court ruled t
 hat Hernandez was not in \ncustody at the CCPO before he received his Mira
 nda warning and that \nhe had knowingly and voluntarily waived his Miranda
  rights \nhttps://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/608us2r52_k5fm.pdf
URL:https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/608us2r52_k5fm.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6d9670ed3e6e0e50@role-professional-responsibility.maine-government-fee
 ds
DTSTAMP:20260909T043942Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Page updated: Maine Board of Overseers of the
  Bar — General News
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + Extended Registration\n  + Attorney license renewal and Guardian ad L
 item license renewal may be completed in the MyBoardAccess portal from Sep
 tember 9 through October 30\, 2026 at 5:00 pm.\n  + Pursuant to M. Bar R. 
 4\,\n  + Registration documents and payments received after August 31st wi
 ll be assessed a non-waivable late fee.\n  + Please note that license rene
 wal requires current contact information\, including a physical residence 
 address\, accurate practice type (private\, government\, judicial\, etc.)\
 , proxy designation for all private practitioners\, and IOLTA account list
 ing or an accurate IOLTA exemption.\n  + If your status has changed since 
 last year (no longer a law clerk\, are retired seeking Inactive\, new judg
 e or seeking to become active again)\, please contact execassistant@mebaro
 verseers.org to request a status change\n  + before you register in the po
 rtal.\n  + Registration is completed online on the\n  + MyBoardAccess\n  +
  by clicking on the Renew Registration section of the Board's web portal.\
 nhttps://www.mebaroverseers.org/
URL:https://www.mebaroverseers.org/
